						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p>&lt;<em><strong>Log Start</strong></em>&gt;</p> <p>Hello, this is Dr. ██████ logging current Research Information for SCP-5156. SCP-5156 appears to be Cognitohazard, that is something to consider as it appears humanoid also. During a test with a Class-D personnel, SCP-5156 appears to be aggravated.</p> <p>Reasons are yet to be discovered. Upon 10 seconds of entering, the Class-D Personnel has been killed and eaten afterwards.</p> <p>Another thing, SCP-5156 looks as if it was growing every day. It was 5'4 before, it is 5'7 now. Considering before was just yesterday, evolution for this entity is fast compared to normal humans.</p> <p>Also, it's capabilities. <strong>Regeneration</strong>. We have managed to grab SCP-5156's DNA and inserted it to a Class-D Personnel. The patient re-grew limbs within seconds of being torn apart. Luckily, it can be put down by shooting it in the head.</p> <p>But, what if it mutates inside the patient making it strong? This could mean easier operations and recontainment. If you think about it, this kind of power could really be implemented to MTF and SD personnel alike. But there is yet a lot to discover. This is Dr. ██████ signing out.</p> <p>&lt;<em><strong>Log End</strong></em>&gt;<br /> &lt;</p> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/alexei-molkov" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7031295&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605818659" alt="Alexei Molkov" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7031295)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/alexei-molkov" >Alexei Molkov</a></span></p> 
